  "id": "Compound::DB01329 - Gene::10864",
  "verbalization": "Cefoperazone is likely to interact with Slc22a7 through a mechanism involving organic anion transport. The evidence suggests that Cefoperazone binds to Slc22a11 or Slc22a8, which are both involved in organic anion transport. Since Slc22a7 is a known participant in this process, it is plausible that Cefoperazone influences Slc22a7 through the organic anion transport pathway. The presence of Oxytetracycline as a binding partner to Slc22a11 further supports this, as it indicates a potential regulatory relationship between antibiotics and transporters. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Cefoperazone in modulating Slc22a7 activity, potentially through the transport of organic anions. This mechanism is supported by the shared involvement of Slc22a7 in the transport of organic anions, suggesting a functional link between Cefoperazone and Slc22a7.",
